[173.656, "o", "{\"advice\":\"I'm not a doctor, but here is a practical week plan. For breakfast, choose oats with plain yoghurt and fruit, or wholemeal toast with egg and tomatoes. For lunch and dinner, use the plate method: 1/2 vegetables/fruit, 1/4 brown rice or wholegrain noodles, and 1/4 fish, chicken, tofu, eggs or beans. Eat regular meals, keep carbohydrate portions modest, and pair them with protein and vegetables. At hawker stalls, choose brown rice where available, two vegetables, one protein and less gravy. Choose water, kopi kosong or teh siew dai instead of sugary drinks. Avoid crash diets. For an indoor morning activity, try the Tuesday 8:30am Morning Chair Strength & Balance session at Woodlands Community Club: 45 minutes, light intensity and suitable for beginners on hazy days. Start gently and stop if you feel dizzy or unusually breathless. Please arrange clinical follow-up for your high screening result.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\"lg-09-hazy-day-activity\",\"lg-06-exercise-by-condition\",\"lg-08-screening-schedule\"],\"rationale\":\"This fits your elevated blood glucose, current activity level of about 3,100 steps a day, high screening risk, and hazy conditions in the North. The food plan supports steadier meals and the indoor activity avoids outdoor haze exposure.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"age_60_64\",\"elevated_blood_glucose\",\"high_screening_risk\",\"low_steps\",\"hazy\",\"Woodlands\"]}\r\n"]
[173.656, "o", "   [PASS ] hosted: valid JSON -- {\"advice\":\"I'm not a doctor, but here is a practical week plan. For breakfast, choose oats with plain yoghurt and fru...\r\n"]
